sequenceDiagram
    actor User as CLI User
    participant RC as RunCommand
    participant Sub as OS Subprocess
    participant S3 as AWS S3
    participant SSM as AWS SSM
    participant EC2 as AWS EC2
    participant DDB as DynamoDB results table
    participant GH as GitHub Releases (laptop only)

    User->>RC: baas run <type> [params] [--instance-type] [--timeout] [--skip-build] [--ami-id]<br/>[--project] [--branch] [--runner-jar] [--tag k=v] [--no-database]
    Note over RC: validate type in {jmh, jmh-with-async, jmh-with-prof, jcstress}<br/>ConfigService.load() from ~/.baas/config.yaml
    Note over RC: an unreleased CLI (0.0.0-semantically-released) names no<br/>release to pin the runner JAR to, so it exits 1 naming<br/>--runner-jar -- before the build and before any upload.
    RC->>Sub: git rev-parse --path-format=absolute --git-common-dir
    Sub-->>RC: repo root -> project name, or "not a git repository"
    Note over RC: resolve project AND results table BEFORE any AWS call.<br/>No --project outside a repo -> exit 1.<br/>No table in config and no --no-database -> exit 1 naming<br/>`baas config sync`. Absent config is never a silent no-op:<br/>discarding measurements takes --no-database by name.
    RC->>Sub: git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD, git rev-parse HEAD
    Sub-->>RC: branch name, commit sha
    RC->>SSM: ssm.getParameter(/<prefix>/runner/ami-id)
    SSM-->>RC: amiId, or ParameterNotFound
    RC->>EC2: ec2.describeImages(amiId)
    EC2-->>RC: image + tags (baas-image-version), or InvalidAMIID.NotFound
    Note over RC: no image -> exit 1 naming `baas admin build-image`.<br/>Deliberately FIRST: before the Maven build and before any<br/>upload, so a missing image costs two API calls.<br/>There is no fallback to AL2023 + yum.
    opt --skip-build = false (default)
        RC->>Sub: mvn clean package -q -DskipTests
        Sub-->>RC: BUILD SUCCESS or RuntimeException on failure
    end
    Note over RC: ONE clock read: runInstant = Instant.now().<br/>runId = RunId.generate(runInstant) -- 20260820T174432812Z-a3f9c21b<br/>resultPath = RunLayout.runPrefix(project, runId)<br/>= runs/&lt;project&gt;/&lt;runId&gt;.<br/>The same instant travels on as --created-at, so the prefix<br/>name and the stored createdAt cannot disagree.
    RC->>S3: s3.putObject(bucket, runs/&lt;project&gt;/&lt;runId&gt;/input/benchmark.jar)
    S3-->>RC: PutObjectResponse
    alt --runner-jar given
        RC->>S3: s3.putObject(bucket, runs/&lt;project&gt;/&lt;runId&gt;/input/runner.jar)
    else pinned to this CLI's own version
        RC->>S3: headObject(releases/&lt;version&gt;/benchmark-runner.jar)
        opt absent
            RC->>GH: GET releases/download/v&lt;version&gt;/benchmark-runner.jar + .sha256
            GH-->>RC: jar + published checksum
            Note over RC: verify, then putObject. A mismatch uploads<br/>nothing and launches nothing. Never overwrites a<br/>present object, so a corrupt one needs deleting.
        end
    end
    Note over RC: buildRunnerTags(): project, commit, branch, type + every --tag.<br/>A --tag naming a machine-observed key (imageVersion,<br/>instanceType, jdk, cpuModel, cpuArch, type) is REJECTED --<br/>those come from the instance, so a result's tags can never<br/>disagree with its own environment.json.
    Note over RC: UserDataScriptBuilder.build() -- installs NOTHING;<br/>the toolchain is baked into the AMI.<br/>Script captures environment.json + packages.txt and uploads<br/>them BEFORE the benchmark, so a crash still leaves a record,<br/>copies benchmark-runner.jar from the bucket -- the instance<br/>reaches NO host outside the account,<br/>carries the results table name in user-data (no credential,<br/>so no SSM round trip -- RunnerRole grants the access),<br/>runs: timeout N java -jar benchmark-runner.jar type<br/>--results-table T (or --no-database) --tag ... <br/>writes run-status sentinel to S3<br/>self-terminates the EC2 instance
    RC->>EC2: ec2.runInstances(amiId, instanceType, subnetId, sgId, instanceProfile, userData, tags)
    Note over EC2: min=1 max=1<br/>shutdownBehavior=TERMINATE<br/>IMDSv2 required<br/>tags: baas-role=benchmark-runner
    EC2-->>RC: instanceId
    Note over RC: register JVM shutdown hook<br/>ec2.terminateInstances(instanceId) on Ctrl+C
    loop poll every 15 seconds
        RC->>S3: s3.getObjectAsBytes(resultPath/run-status)
        S3-->>RC: completed or failed:N or absent -- sleep 15s and retry
    end
    Note over RC: --no-database: nothing was stored, so nothing to show.<br/>A benchmark that already ran is never reported as failed<br/>because the summary could not be fetched.
    RC->>DDB: Query on requestId-index (gsi1pk = runId)
    DDB-->>RC: one item per measurement
    RC-->>User: print BENCHMARK | REQUEST_ID | TYPE | MODE | SCORE | ERROR | UNIT and exit 0<br/>naming the runId, which is what `baas download &lt;runId&gt;` takes
